# DataFlow Medallion: Spark, Airflow & dbt
This project is a data engineering pet project that demonstrates the design of a hybrid data platform (Cloud + Local) using widely adopted tools and practices:

## AWS S3 as the Data Lake (Bronze layer).

Spark for parallel batch processing and streaming (Bronze → Silver → Gold).

Airflow for orchestration of batch pipelines and integration with dbt.

dbt for SQL-based modeling and transformations in the Silver and Gold layers.

Terraform for infrastructure provisioning as code.

Snowflake (trial) or DuckDB as the Data Warehouse.

Metabase/Power BI for data visualization.

## 🎯 Purpose
The project explores modern data architectures and best practices in ingestion, transformation, and visualization, with emphasis on:

Parallelism: ingesting multiple APIs (e.g., Airbnb data from several European capitals).

Near real-time streaming: open datasets such as weather, air quality, and UV radiation.

Medallion architecture (Bronze, Silver, Gold): clear and scalable data organization.

Infrastructure as Code: reproducibility and governance.

🚀 Outcomes
Documented batch and streaming pipelines.

Near real-time dashboards or Dashboards enriched with different datasets.

Minimal costs (< US$ 2/month) using sample datasets and small clusters.

Complete documentation to serve as a reference for experimentation and testing.